is documented that the shape of the ring is extremely close, albeit not exactly
identical, to the true ellipse of an identical major and minor axes. The likely
knowledge of ellipses possessed by the ring’s maker is identified. In the 
paper, a detailed [...] 1. The Ring of Nestor, measuring 3.29 cm by 2.18 cm, is
the fifth largest Aegean signet ring.\n2. Research confirms its authenticity, 
contrasting earlier claims of forgery by scholars in the 1920s.\n3. The 
